title: Linux Bubblewrap Lifecycle and Limits Tasks
status: implemented
created: 2026-10-31
author: adrian
items[7]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,"[x] Copy the baseline","Copy `adrs/2026-10-31-linux-bwrap-sandbox/poc` into this ADR unchanged and commit it before extending.","The copied tree is byte-identical to the isolation PoC by construction; the isolation ADR records its tests.",low,0.5h,,"shared-code"
  T-002,"[x] Cgroup launcher","Wrap the harness in `systemd-run --user --scope --unit=lbx-<pid>` with `--new-session`, and detect a missing user manager with `systemctl --user show-environment`.","The scope is active and the workload runs in its own session; the missing-manager path exits 69.",medium,2h,T-001,"session-by-default,systemd-optional"
  T-003,"[x] Freeze and thaw","Freeze the scope with `systemctl --user freeze` and resume with `systemctl --user thaw`; assert the loop file stops and restarts.","Frozen byte count is unchanged, thawed count grows, and the scope is stopped after thaw. `unfreeze` is not a systemd verb and is not used.",medium,2h,T-002,"cgroup-freeze,freeze-and-resume"
  T-004,"[x] Resource limits","Run a memory hog and a thread hog under `MemoryMax` and `TasksMax`; assert both fail. CPUQuota is not applied.","Both workloads exit non-zero and the host remains responsive.",medium,2h,T-002,"resource-limits,memory-limit,task-limit"
  T-005,"[x] Fallback script","Keep the copied `lifecycle.sh` as the process-group path. Selection was exercised with `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/nonexistent`: `lifecycle-cgroup.sh` exits 69 and `lifecycle.sh` freezes, resumes and kills.","The launcher selects the fallback and the script records freeze, resume and group kill.",low,1h,T-001,"process-group-fallback,fallback,systemd-absent"
  T-006,"[x] Launcher cost","Measure the `systemd-run --user --scope` startup cost against the direct harness path.","Median and p95 recorded: direct 23.8/26.4ms, scope 47.5/56.2ms.",low,1h,T-002,"cost-recorded"
  T-007,"[x] Findings","Record the cgroup properties, freeze results, limit results, costs and remaining risks.","Every verified acceptance criterion has an observation with the command and output.",medium,2h,"T-002,T-003,T-004,T-005","tests"
